{"timestamp":"2026-05-19T17:56:26.206Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Prompt file paths can escape the repo and mutate arbitrary parent files\",\"category\":\"security\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"e2e/vogon/main.go\",\"startLine\":176,\"endLine\":186,\"symbol\":\"createFileRe/modifyFileRe/deleteFileRe\",\"quote\":\"([^\\u001fs,]+\\\\.(?:` + fileExt + `))\"},{\"path\":\"e2e/vogon/main.go\",\"startLine\":485,\"endLine\":507,\"symbol\":\"createFile/modifyFile/deleteFile\",\"quote\":\"abs := filepath.Join(dir, path)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The prompt regexes accept any non-space path ending in an allowed extension, including parent-relative paths such as ../victim.txt. The file operations then join that untrusted path to the current directory and call WriteFile or Remove without cleaning and verifying that the result remains inside the repo. A prompt like `delete ../victim.txt` can remove a sibling file before git add ever has a chance to reject an out-of-repo path.\",\"reproduction\":\"From a temp repo with a sibling `victim.txt`, run `vogon -p \\\"delete ../victim.txt\\\"`; the sibling file is removed because the parsed action path is passed directly to `os.Remove(filepath.Join(dir, path))`.\",\"recommendation\":\"Add a single action-path sanitizer that rejects absolute paths, cleaned paths equal to `..` or starting with `../`, and paths that resolve outside the repo root. Use the sanitized repo-relative path for create, modify, delete, and git add.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"No linked tests were provided for this feature, and the sampled Vogon E2E prompts use normal in-repo paths rather than traversal paths.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a Vogon test that executes create/modify/delete actions with `../outside.txt` and asserts the outside file is unchanged and the command exits nonzero or reports a rejected path.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Validate action paths at the boundary before any filesystem mutation in `executeActions` or in each file operation helper.\"},{\"title\":\"Hook and git failures are logged but still produce a successful agent run\",\"category\":\"bug\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"e2e/vogon/main.go\",\"startLine\":521,\"endLine\":532,\"symbol\":\"gitRun\",\"quote\":\"if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil { fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \\\"git %s: %v\\\\n\\\", strings.Join(args, \\\" \\\"), err) }\"},{\"path\":\"e2e/vogon/main.go\",\"startLine\":537,\"endLine\":552,\"symbol\":\"fireHook\",\"quote\":\"if err != nil { fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \\\"hook %s failed: %v\\\\n%s\\\\n\\\", hookName, err, out) }\"},{\"path\":\"e2e/vogon/main.go\",\"startLine\":140,\"endLine\":160,\"symbol\":\"runTurn\",\"quote\":null}],\"reasoning\":\"Vogon is the deterministic E2E canary for the hook and checkpoint lifecycle, so hook and git failures are core failures of the command. Today `fireHook` and `gitRun` only print errors and return, while `runTurn` continues and `main` exits 0 unless an unrelated fatal path is hit. If `entire hooks` is missing or a git commit fails, the harness can see a successful agent invocation even though the lifecycle was not exercised correctly.\",\"reproduction\":\"Run Vogon in an environment where `entire hooks vogon session-start` fails, for example with `entire` absent from PATH. The command prints hook errors to stderr but continues through the prompt and exits successfully.\",\"recommendation\":\"Make `fireHook`, `gitRun`, `gitCommit`, and `executeActions` return errors. Propagate those errors through `runTurn` to `main` and call `fatal` so failed hooks or git operations produce a nonzero exit.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"No linked tests were provided for this feature, and existing prompt-oriented E2E coverage generally asserts resulting files/checkpoints rather than directly asserting Vogon exits nonzero when hooks or git operations fail.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a test that runs Vogon with PATH arranged so `entire hooks` fails and asserts a nonzero exit code; add a second test for a failing git commit path if practical.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Change error handling in the hook/git execution path and update callers to stop the run on failure.\"}],\"inspected\":{\"files\":[\"e2e/vogon/main.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/execx/execx.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/execx/execx_unix.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/execx/execx_windows.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/vogon/vogon.go\",\"e2e/agents/vogon.go\",\"e2e/tests/edge_cases_test.go\",\"e2e/tests/stash_workflows_test.go\",\"e2e/tests/checkpoint_metadata_test.go\",\"e2e/tests/session_lifecycle_test.go\"],\"symbols\":[\"main\",\"parseArgs\",\"validateSessionID\",\"runTurn\",\"parsePrompt\",\"parseNumberedSteps\",\"executeActions\",\"createFile\",\"modifyFile\",\"deleteFile\",\"gitCommit\",\"gitRun\",\"fireHook\",\"setupTranscript\",\"appendTranscript\",\"execx.NonInteractive\",\"execx.detachFromTTY\"],\"notes\":[\"Used code-reviewer skill guidance for a findings-first static review.\",\"Feature metadata listed no linked tests; sampled Vogon E2E usages to understand intended prompt shapes.\",\"Did not run tests; sandbox is read-only and Go could not create its build cache.\"]}}","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
